00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.110
Nicole: As we have already mentioned
the skills needed to be a cyber

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:08.750
security professional are a combination
of both hard and soft skills.

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:13.389
Diverse experiences of all areas
of a business can give that extra

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:15.170
help beyond the technical skills.

00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:19.140
Understanding human psychology
can help when identifying issues

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.790
with social engineering threats.

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:25.230
Abraham: Project management and team
work along with marketing and PR

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.560
skills can also help a cyber security
professional working with a range of

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.230
different projects and departments.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:35.269
Nicole: Let’s look at the range of skills
that are advantageous for those who wish

00:00:35.269 --> 00:00:37.570
to work as cyber security professionals.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.480
Cyber security is not just a
problem that affects one area

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.430
of a company or an organisation.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.899
Most departments today rely on
digital communication and technology

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:51.249
and are therefore liable to be
vulnerable to a cyber breach.

00:00:51.809 --> 00:00:54.640
Abraham: Cyber security professionals
will be called upon to resolve

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.770
issues across a range of areas making
good use of interpersonal skills.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.540
Nicole: Interpersonal skills include a
variety of different skills including

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.729
the ability to listen to others and
respect their views and communicate

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.220
well both verbally and non-verbally.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.330
They also involve working well and
collaborating with others whilst being

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.830
both self-aware and showing empathy.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.460
Abraham: The ability to be able to
ask the right questions and give out

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.870
the relevant information are really
important in cyber security, as

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.949
are giving and receiving feedback.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:31.480
Cyber security professionals have
to interact with staff at all levels

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:35.220
and educate others on the threats
an organisation may be open to.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.990
Nicole: Critical thinking helps a cyber
security professional to be able to

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:44.600
be able to detect and troubleshoot any
problems or potential vulnerabilities.

00:01:45.089 --> 00:01:50.070
It is the process of objective analysis
and evaluation of an issue to help with

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.470
decision making and includes using skills
of observation, experience and reflection.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.310
Abraham: Attention to detail can
help a cyber security professional

00:01:59.599 --> 00:02:02.870
with identifying potential
issues, whilst continuously

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.719
monitoring networks and systems.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:08.410
Being able to defend an
organisation involves being highly

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:10.220
vigilant and detail oriented.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:15.609
Nicole: A Strong Technical Knowledge Base
is one of the most obvious skill areas.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.039
And it is not surprising that many cyber
security experts started out hacking!

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:23.759
It is important to know a system
fully to be able to understand

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.720
how it can be exploited.

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:30.390
Essentially a cyber security professional
needs to have the same skills as a

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.070
Hacker, but not the same inclinations.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.040
Abraham: This can involve practical
hands-on techniques and more

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.610
conceptual technical knowledge.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:43.320
Practical skills consist of the
ability to configure a network, conduct

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.500
a pen test or instal a firewall.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.040
Nicole: Conceptual technical knowledge
involves everything from knowing how

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.510
to code and a variety of programming
languages to knowing how to subnet.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.899
Abraham: Being able to code
using languages such as HTML and

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:03.589
JavaScript, can help to understand how
applications and websites are made and

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.380
therefore how they can be exploited.

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:09.070
Learning how to develop scripts
in languages like Python

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:12.340
can help to understand core
processes in potential roles.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:19.710
Learning the intricacies of setting up
networks, LAN, WAN and VPN, can help gain

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:24.160
skills needed by many organisations and
businesses in their everyday operations.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:29.380
Nicole: The ability to run, configure
and maintain common applications such as

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:35.029
databases and webservers are always in
demand as software and other applications

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:37.060
are integral tools for businesses.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.970
Systems are key in cyber security,
so it is important to have a good

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:46.870
knowledge of desktop and mobile systems
including common operating systems.

00:03:47.509 --> 00:03:52.019
Abraham: Cyber security as with all
technology is constantly changing and

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:56.079
cyber security professionals need to stay
at the top of the curve and therefore

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:59.880
must keep up to date with the latest
industry trends and best practices.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.579
Nicole: Essentially a cyber
security professional needs to

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.260
have the same technical skills
or better, than a ‘Hacker’, to

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.810
be able to thwart their attacks.

00:04:09.309 --> 00:04:12.300
Abraham: This often involves
educating themselves both during

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.410
working hours and in their own time.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:18.490
It is a major commitment, but
it can also be very rewarding.

